# Ral, Crackling Wit: "Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, put a loyalty counter on Ral." Ral enters with 4 (casting him
# is not a spell cast with him on the battlefield). Bot2 casts two noncreature spells in its own turn (Mox Jet, Mox Sapphire):
# not "you", so no counter. Bot1 casts Ornithopter (a creature spell, an artifact creature): no counter. Bot1 casts Lightning
# Bolt: Ral gets a counter and the Otter token's prowess (a noncreature spell) makes it 2/2 until end of turn. Bot2 counters the
# Bolt, and Ral keeps the counter: the trigger resolves before the spell and is independent of it (the ruling).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Ral, Crackling Wit
Ornithopter
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Counterspell
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ral, Crackling Wit.Cast
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ral, Crackling Wit.Counters.Loyalty = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Ral, Crackling Wit.Activate(Ability: Create a 1/1)
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ral, Crackling Wit.Counters.Loyalty = 5
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ral, Crackling Wit.Counters.Loyalty = 5
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Triggers(Ral, Crackling Wit; Otter Token)
? Stack.Count = 3
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Stack.Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ral, Crackling Wit.Counters.Loyalty = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Otter Token.Power = 2
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Graveyard = Counterspell
